00:42:52,601 --> 00:42:55,000
of cover, a place where you've seen a lot of game, you can press

763
00:42:55,001 --> 00:42:57,800
a waypoint, mark that point, you know how to get back there.

764
00:42:57,801 --> 00:43:01,020
So it's very much a safety device.

765
00:43:01,021 --> 00:43:04,020
The 12-channel receiver comes loaded with a base map that

766
00:43:04,021 --> 00:43:08,920
displays specific topographical features, such as mountains,

767
00:43:08,921 --> 00:43:14,960
trees, and roads. A 5.3-ounce receiver like this

768
00:43:14,961 --> 00:43:21,680
one has a battery life of up to 18 hours and can download even more detailed maps from CD-ROM.

769
00:43:21,681 --> 00:43:28,120
It is accurate to within 10 feet. The GPS and all these other modern tools

770
00:43:28,121 --> 00:43:35,680
and techniques are part of a sophisticated industry that has replicated the sights, sounds,

771
00:43:35,681 --> 00:43:40,180
and smells of wildlife, managed the quantity and quality

772
00:43:40,280 --> 00:43:42,820
of game, and honed our hunting gear

773
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:46,520
to perform within inches and milliseconds.

774
00:43:46,620 --> 00:43:49,700
The development of these weapons has granted us godlike powers

775
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:55,360
of control, responsibility, and fate over the Earth's animals.

776
00:43:55,460 --> 00:43:58,340
How wisely we use future hunting technology

777
00:43:58,440 --> 00:44:01,580
and foster game conservation will determine

778
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:05,280
the delicate balance between predator and prey

779
00:44:05,281 --> 00:44:08,240
that has existed for millennia.

